# A KVM guest gives cold page cache back to its host (ops#10nov-2123): the kernel's LRU knows which file pages
# nobody used lately (the inactive file list); this asks it to drop them, beyond 1 GiB kept, at most 1 GiB a run
# (cache-trim.timer: every minute), file pages only (swappiness=0). Free page reporting (the host's memballoon
# freePageReporting='on') hands the freed pages to the host. DAMON_RECLAIM (damon-reclaim.service) turned out
# too coarse for this: one access in a 26 MB region keeps it warm.
[Unit]
Description=Trim cold page cache back to the KVM host
ConditionPathExists=/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.reclaim

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'i=$$(awk "/^Inactive\\(file\\):/{print \\$$2}" /proc/meminfo); n=$$((i - 1048576)); [ $$n -gt 65536 ] || exit 0; [ $$n -gt 1048576 ] && n=1048576; echo "$${n}K swappiness=0" >/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.reclaim || true'
